WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:02.978
<v Examiner>Exam case 13, continued.

2
00:00:02.978 --> 00:00:07.618
<v Examiner>Contraception, and the three starred questions she hasn't answered yet.

3
00:00:08.068 --> 00:00:08.873
<v Examiner>Three marks.

4
00:00:08.873 --> 00:00:14.102
<v Examiner>Hormonal methods of contraception tend to affect a female's fertility by using

5
00:00:14.102 --> 00:00:14.974
<v Examiner>progesterone.

6
00:00:14.974 --> 00:00:19.801
<v Examiner>How do we use the normal functions of progesterone to prevent pregnancy?

7
00:00:20.251 --> 00:00:23.857
The hook: stop ovulation, block the sperm, fake a pregnancy.

8
00:00:24.307 --> 00:00:28.143
It prevents ovulation, by stopping LH from being released.

9
00:00:28.143 --> 00:00:31.980
It thickens the cervical mucus, which keeps the sperm out.

10
00:00:31.980 --> 00:00:36.147
And it imitates pregnancy, by keeping progesterone levels high.

11
00:00:37.597 --> 00:00:38.290
<v Examiner>Six marks.

12
00:00:38.290 --> 00:00:41.477
<v Examiner>Contraception can be hormonal or non-hormonal.

13
00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:46.744
<v Examiner>Summarise the differences in a table: the method, how it prevents pregnancy,

14
00:00:46.744 --> 00:00:48.754
<v Examiner>and whether it prevents STIs.

15
00:00:49.204 --> 00:00:55.391
The hook: hormones stop ovulation, a condom is a barrier, and only the condom stops STIs.

16
00:00:55.841 --> 00:00:56.931
Hormonal methods.

17
00:00:56.931 --> 00:01:01.423
The pill, and the Jadelle implant, which slowly releases the hormones,

18
00:01:01.423 --> 00:01:03.797
may prevent ovulation from happening.

19
00:01:03.797 --> 00:01:06.492
The mini pill, which is progesterone only,

20
00:01:06.492 --> 00:01:09.636
prevents ovulation by stopping LH being released,

21
00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:12.844
thickens the cervical mucus to keep the sperm out,

22
00:01:12.844 --> 00:01:16.181
and imitates pregnancy by keeping progesterone high.

23
00:01:16.181 --> 00:01:18.299
Do hormonal methods prevent STIs?

24
00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:18.491
No.

25
00:01:18.491 --> 00:01:19.454
Pregnancy only.

26
00:01:19.454 --> 00:01:20.673
There's no barrier.

27
00:01:21.123 --> 00:01:22.462
Non-hormonal methods.

28
00:01:22.462 --> 00:01:27.691
Condoms form a barrier that prevents the semen from getting into the woman's body.

29
00:01:27.691 --> 00:01:32.792
They protect against both pregnancy and STIs, like gonorrhoea, syphilis and HIV.

30
00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:37.511
But not pubic lice, which live in the pubic hair the condom doesn't cover.

31
00:01:37.511 --> 00:01:41.910
The IUD may prevent implantation of the conceptus in the endometrium,

32
00:01:41.910 --> 00:01:44.397
and it protects against pregnancy only.

33
00:01:44.847 --> 00:01:49.467
Filing the IUD under non-hormonal is the Paper Sim's own reading,

34
00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.026
because some IUDs do carry hormones.

35
00:01:52.026 --> 00:01:58.138
But her session's point stands either way: only the condom also protects against STIs.

36
00:01:59.588 --> 00:02:03.355
<v Examiner>Now the three starred questions she hasn't posted answers to.

37
00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:07.740
<v Examiner>They're still fair game in the exam, so here's a sound answer for each,

38
00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:09.593
<v Examiner>built from her module content.

39
00:02:10.043 --> 00:02:10.292
<v Examiner>One.

40
00:02:10.292 --> 00:02:12.780
<v Examiner>Male and female fertility are different.

41
00:02:12.780 --> 00:02:16.635
<v Examiner>What are some of the key factors in male and female fertility?

42
00:02:17.085 --> 00:02:21.218
For a male: enough sperm, that move well and are the right shape.

43
00:02:21.218 --> 00:02:25.477
The hormones that drive sperm production: FSH, LH and testosterone.

44
00:02:25.477 --> 00:02:29.164
And testes kept a little cooler than the rest of the body,

45
00:02:29.164 --> 00:02:31.516
which is why they sit in the scrotum.

46
00:02:31.516 --> 00:02:36.157
For a female: age, because the number and quality of eggs fall over time.

47
00:02:36.157 --> 00:02:41.116
Regular ovulation, which needs FSH, LH, oestrogen and progesterone in balance.

48
00:02:41.116 --> 00:02:44.421
Open fallopian tubes, so the egg and sperm can meet.

49
00:02:44.421 --> 00:02:47.346
And a healthy uterine lining for implantation.

50
00:02:47.346 --> 00:02:49.571
For both: smoking, alcohol, weight,

51
00:02:49.571 --> 00:02:53.830
stress and sexually transmitted infections can all lower fertility.

52
00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.280
And for Rose: after Depo Provera, her cycle can take months to return.

53
00:02:59.730 --> 00:02:59.956
<v Examiner>Two.

54
00:02:59.956 --> 00:03:03.399
<v Examiner>What are the functions of the sex hormones in the human body?

55
00:03:03.849 --> 00:03:06.363
You already have this one, from Test 3.

56
00:03:06.363 --> 00:03:11.134
FSH grows the follicles in a female, and drives spermatogenesis in a male.

57
00:03:11.134 --> 00:03:14.357
LH triggers ovulation and forms the corpus luteum,

58
00:03:14.357 --> 00:03:18.289
and in a male it makes the Leydig cells produce testosterone.

59
00:03:18.289 --> 00:03:23.447
Oestrogen drives follicle growth, grows the reproductive organs and the breasts,

60
00:03:23.447 --> 00:03:26.025
lays fat on the hips, widens the pelvis,

61
00:03:26.025 --> 00:03:29.635
and rebuilds the endometrium in the proliferative phase.

62
00:03:29.635 --> 00:03:34.663
Progesterone readies the endometrium for implantation, in the secretory phase,

63
00:03:34.663 --> 00:03:37.564
and develops the breast alveoli in pregnancy.

64
00:03:37.564 --> 00:03:42.915
And testosterone drives spermatogenesis and the male secondary sex characteristics:

65
00:03:42.915 --> 00:03:45.300
more muscle, denser bone, and libido.

66
00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:47.190
<v Examiner>Three.

67
00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:51.227
<v Examiner>Injections of the hormone FSH usually form part of IVF.

68
00:03:51.227 --> 00:03:57.758
<v Examiner>What is IVF, when would it be appropriate, and what is the purpose of the FSH injections?

69
00:03:58.208 --> 00:04:00.136
IVF is in vitro fertilisation.

70
00:04:00.136 --> 00:04:04.314
In vitro means in glass: the eggs are collected from the ovaries,

71
00:04:04.314 --> 00:04:08.877
fertilised by sperm in a lab, and the embryo is placed into the uterus.

72
00:04:08.877 --> 00:04:13.055
It's appropriate when the fallopian tubes are blocked or damaged,

73
00:04:13.055 --> 00:04:18.197
when the sperm count or movement is low, with ovulation problems, endometriosis,

74
00:04:18.197 --> 00:04:22.696
or unexplained infertility, or when simpler treatments haven't worked.

75
00:04:22.696 --> 00:04:27.516
The FSH injections stimulate the ovaries to grow several follicles at once,

76
00:04:27.516 --> 00:04:29.637
instead of the usual one a month.

77
00:04:29.637 --> 00:04:33.236
Her session says FSH is for the growth of the follicles.

78
00:04:33.236 --> 00:04:38.571
More follicles means more eggs to collect, and a better chance of a healthy embryo.

79
00:04:39.021 --> 00:04:39.629
<v Examiner>Once more.

80
00:04:39.629 --> 00:04:42.306
<v Examiner>Contraception, and the three open questions.

81
00:04:44.756 --> 00:04:48.557
Progesterone contraception stops ovulation by blocking LH,

82
00:04:48.557 --> 00:04:53.145
thickens the cervical mucus to keep sperm out, and imitates pregnancy.

83
00:04:53.145 --> 00:04:59.044
Hormonal methods, the pill, the Jadelle implant and the mini pill, prevent pregnancy only.

84
00:04:59.044 --> 00:05:04.746
Condoms are a barrier, and the only method that also stops STIs, though not pubic lice.

85
00:05:04.746 --> 00:05:08.809
The IUD may prevent implantation, and prevents pregnancy only.

86
00:05:08.809 --> 00:05:13.790
Fertility needs healthy sperm and hormones in a male, and regular ovulation,

87
00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:16.674
open tubes and a healthy lining in a female.

88
00:05:16.674 --> 00:05:20.934
IVF fertilises eggs in a lab and places the embryo in the uterus,

89
00:05:20.934 --> 00:05:26.505
and the FSH injections grow several follicles at once, so more eggs can be collected.
